{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01JW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5394977cf59996cc2bc7a53f1ca34f48c3ec2983bb9054bba25ec359346affcf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc63b02a56f62d3107c5ac6896b7aba56c8ba1b0d9a790350aead0adf2478612", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an\nimmersion (resp.<SPACE_0001>closed immersion, resp. open immersion)\nof schemes over <MATH_0003>. Then any base change of <MATH_0004> is an\nimmersion (resp.<SPACE_0002>closed immersion, resp. open immersion).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec18e4680446078b8e0149f7645138299003aab48183a05abcc6c4fd24ee29eb", "unit_id": "tag:01JY:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01JW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX_{S'} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\ar@/^4ex/[dd] \\\\\nY_{S'} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & Y \\ar[d] \\\\\nS' \\ar[r] & S\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X_{S'} \\cong Y_{S'} \\times_Y X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:55239bd406a87c39922cf46ce3e4a5e3c0d4dd86105d473e782d4514d2b3b966", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82f9a76b4e424214d84e249c7a79a374d9c5ac090cdb0209008ea73e28584054", "source_text": "We can think of the base change of <MATH_0001> via the morphism\n<MATH_0002> as the top left vertical arrow in the following\ncommutative diagram:\n<MATH_0003>\nThe diagram implies <MATH_0004>,\nand the lemma follows from Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:548894bd2c27a7285b22eaccdf14e1f89c50e6e00848c87656a433811de4dd16", "unit_id": "tag:01JY:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01JW", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:799d7c2122cff469ddfc0e493962bb026757b9f8827be8d9867f8e4816dc7921", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn fact this type of result is so typical that there is a\npiece of language to express it. Here it is.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d5dcd85171a8e9ed189dc2622cf45f2f3a80f9a970b45c546d4e5b14bd05f0a", "unit_id": "tag:01JW:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01JW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0004": "$X/S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0006": "$X_{S'}/S'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0010": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0013": "$f' : X_{S'} \\to Y_{S'}$", "MATH_0014": "$S'$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-preserved-by-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cdda62553d6d27fa53833e1c8dd89e9e10083fecb95721e568b1201a0b20abec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4006bed41b1d02697dbf46cbaab548a042d7692363a8238829a1d41521118e25", "source_text": "Properties and base change.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0001> be a property of schemes over a base.\nWe say that <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>preserved under arbitrary base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>,\nor simply that <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>preserved under base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif whenever <MATH_0004>\nhas <MATH_0005>, any base change <MATH_0006> has <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0008> be a property of morphisms of schemes over a base.\nWe say that <MATH_0009> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>preserved under arbitrary base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>,\nor simply that <TEXTITOPEN_0004>preserved under base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> if whenever\n<MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011> has <MATH_0012>, any base change\n<MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014> has <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:86bbfe80a6135d58ed9e27f7cf7f7d9ce56aa03ed0f2051ef14f403ac46b6f4d", "unit_id": "tag:01JZ:statement"}
